<title>USA: Chiron Q4 Betaseron sales decline.</title>
<headline>Chiron Q4 Betaseron sales decline.</headline>
<dateline>EMERYVILLE, Calif. 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chiron Corp, which earlier reported higher company wide sales in its fourth quarter, said sales of its Betaseron multiple sclerosis drug declined to $17.3 million from $25 million.</p>
<p>It said the drop was due mainly to lower shipments to Berlex Laboratories, Schering AG's U.S. affiliate, which is distributing the drug.</p>
<p>The fourth quarter Beraseron sales compare with third quarter sales of $16.8 million. The drug's launch was disrupted in the second quarter, when Chiron had to reword a packaging insert, delaying shipments.</p>
</text>
